1
00:00:06,465 --> 00:00:07,924
<i>Previously on</i> Reacher...

2
00:00:07,925 --> 00:00:09,510
No one can help me now.

3
00:00:10,636 --> 00:00:12,178
[Docherty] <i>This is Detective Tamara Green.</i>

4
00:00:12,179 --> 00:00:13,346
[Tamara] We got a call some other people

5
00:00:13,347 --> 00:00:14,973
<i>- want to ask you some questions.</i>
- [Reacher] <i>What is it the government's</i>

6
00:00:14,974 --> 00:00:16,391
so worried she might have given me?

7
00:00:16,392 --> 00:00:18,518
<i>- What are you looking for?</i>
- The flash drive.

8
00:00:18,519 --> 00:00:19,602
Who's your boss?

9
00:00:19,603 --> 00:00:20,603
I'm Lila.

10
00:00:20,604 --> 00:00:22,772
She promised to do all she could
to find my father, and she did.

11
00:00:22,773 --> 00:00:24,190
Someone important.

12
00:00:24,191 --> 00:00:25,900
Congressman John Sampson.

13
00:00:25,901 --> 00:00:27,444
You're gonna blackmail him
with information

14
00:00:27,445 --> 00:00:29,070
Anna stole for you from the Pentagon.

15
00:00:29,071 --> 00:00:30,947
<i>Jacob. How'd your nephew take the news?</i>

16
00:00:30,948 --> 00:00:31,990
I didn't track him down yet.

17
00:00:31,991 --> 00:00:33,408
Seems your sister may have
stolen some confidential data--

18
00:00:33,409 --> 00:00:34,743
Where are you going?

19
00:00:34,744 --> 00:00:36,203
[Jacob] <i>I want to find out all I can
about John Sampson.</i>

20
00:00:37,246 --> 00:00:38,329
[Reacher] <i>Okay.</i>

21
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:39,706
- Let's go.
- You're coming?

22
00:00:39,707 --> 00:00:41,040
I'm good at not letting people

23
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:42,292
<i>get away with things.</i>

24
00:00:42,293 --> 00:00:44,377
[grunting]

25
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:47,005
[exciting music playing]

26
00:00:47,006 --> 00:00:47,964
[Foster] Take him.

27
00:00:47,965 --> 00:00:49,633
[grunting]

28
00:01:01,687 --> 00:01:03,063
[pulsing music playing]

29
00:01:04,315 --> 00:01:06,317
[Reacher grunting softly]

30
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,325
Oh.

31
00:01:15,326 --> 00:01:16,452
Shoot.

32
00:01:24,585 --> 00:01:26,837
Welcome to the party.

33
00:01:30,841 --> 00:01:32,509
How long was I out?

34
00:01:32,510 --> 00:01:34,011
No idea.

35
00:01:35,095 --> 00:01:37,430
You were here when we woke up
a couple hours ago.

36
00:01:37,431 --> 00:01:40,558
They shot me with a tranquilizer dart.

37
00:01:40,559 --> 00:01:42,061
Twice.

38
00:01:43,145 --> 00:01:44,312
How'd they get you?

39
00:01:44,313 --> 00:01:45,814
Hey.

40
00:01:45,815 --> 00:01:47,232
Big Brother's watching.

41
00:01:47,233 --> 00:01:49,150
Probably listening, too.

42
00:01:49,151 --> 00:01:51,487
They already know how you got here.

43
00:01:52,905 --> 00:01:54,490
No harm in telling me.

44
00:01:55,407 --> 00:01:57,785
I got home,
soon as I put my gun in my safe.

45
00:01:58,994 --> 00:02:01,204
Someone must have been
hiding in my house.

46
00:02:01,205 --> 00:02:03,039
Smelled some chloroform.

47
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,249
Here I am.

48
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:05,875
I was walking to the bus stop
near my house

49
00:02:05,876 --> 00:02:07,544
to meet up with you in New York,

50
00:02:07,545 --> 00:02:09,671
felt a sting in my chest,

51
00:02:09,672 --> 00:02:11,965
looked down and there was a dart.

52
00:02:11,966 --> 00:02:14,259
Next thing I know, I'm looking at

53
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:16,136
leaves on trees...

54
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:18,806
Then I wake up here.

55
00:02:20,641 --> 00:02:22,183
I'm the only one who's tied down.

56
00:02:22,184 --> 00:02:24,353
Yeah. Have you seen yourself?

57
00:02:25,688 --> 00:02:27,105
Neither of us got a look at them.

58
00:02:27,106 --> 00:02:29,691
Have any idea who grabbed us?

59
00:02:29,692 --> 00:02:31,694
Maybe the guys
who took a run at you yesterday?

60
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:33,945
CIA.

61
00:02:33,946 --> 00:02:35,238
They told you that?

62
00:02:35,239 --> 00:02:37,407
Didn't need to.

63
00:02:37,408 --> 00:02:39,576
They didn't Mirandize us,
cite the Patriot Act

64
00:02:39,577 --> 00:02:41,661
or gin up any charges.

65
00:02:41,662 --> 00:02:43,663
Means they don't have the power to arrest.

66
00:02:43,664 --> 00:02:45,915
But they had no problem
drugging, kidnapping

67
00:02:45,916 --> 00:02:47,959
and locking us up
in what I can only imagine

68
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:51,212
is a basement, considering the smell
and lack of natural light.

69
00:02:51,213 --> 00:02:53,631
What federal agency
best fits that description?

70
00:02:53,632 --> 00:02:57,093
I thought the CIA wasn't supposed
to operate on U.S. soil.

71
00:02:57,094 --> 00:02:59,095
This shit's crazy.
'Cause abducting some drifter

72
00:02:59,096 --> 00:03:02,098
is one thing-- no offense--
but snatching up cops?

73
00:03:02,099 --> 00:03:03,434
So what does it all mean?

74
00:03:04,518 --> 00:03:06,603
- Means we're fucked.
- [door opens]

75
00:03:06,604 --> 00:03:08,606
[menacing music playing]

76
00:03:16,071 --> 00:03:18,073
[keypad beeping]

77
00:03:22,453 --> 00:03:25,330
- What's that?
- A stimulant. To clear your head.

78
00:03:25,331 --> 00:03:26,748
It's clear.

79
00:03:26,749 --> 00:03:28,249
I just do what they tell me.

80
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:31,169
They tell you to get that needle
jammed in your eye?

81
00:03:31,170 --> 00:03:33,671
'Cause that's what's gonna happen,
you try and stick me with that.

82
00:03:33,672 --> 00:03:35,382
Sounds like he's plenty awake.

83
00:03:36,467 --> 00:03:37,968
Forget the shot, Doc.

84
00:03:40,387 --> 00:03:41,471
How's your neck?

85
00:03:41,472 --> 00:03:43,556
How's your head?

86
00:03:43,557 --> 00:03:45,768
Hear that tranq hangovers can be a bitch.

87
00:03:49,772 --> 00:03:51,356
Good luck trying to get those on me.

88
00:03:51,357 --> 00:03:52,982
Oh, they're going on.

89
00:03:52,983 --> 00:03:55,444
Question is are they going on
the easy way or the hard way?

90
00:03:59,531 --> 00:04:01,658
We upped the dose.

91
00:04:01,659 --> 00:04:03,618
So, you want to be a hard-ass

92
00:04:03,619 --> 00:04:06,079
or you want to get this over with,
Mr. Reacher?

93
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:08,457
Just Reacher.

94
00:04:28,811 --> 00:04:30,312
[door closes]

95
00:04:38,988 --> 00:04:41,614
[Foster] Jack Reacher. No middle name.

96
00:04:41,615 --> 00:04:43,575
Parents couldn't be bothered?

97
00:04:45,244 --> 00:04:48,162
What sort of given name is Jack?
Jack's a nickname.

98
00:04:48,163 --> 00:04:50,499
Why don't you tell me your names
and we can compare.

99
00:04:53,168 --> 00:04:54,293
Okay.

100
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:55,586
You're Wynken,

101
00:04:55,587 --> 00:04:57,338
he's Blynken, that's Nod.

102
00:04:57,339 --> 00:04:59,257
From the Dutch lullaby.

103
00:04:59,258 --> 00:05:01,259
You call us that
because we put you to sleep?

104
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:03,219
I call you that because,
before I leave this room,

105
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:04,805
I'm gonna put all of you to sleep.

106
00:05:14,231 --> 00:05:17,025
Our techs combed through the data,
and the only thing that's on there

107
00:05:17,026 --> 00:05:20,987
is some student's mediocre sketches.

108
00:05:20,988 --> 00:05:22,363
Why?

109
00:05:22,364 --> 00:05:24,574
Maybe he doesn't apply himself.

110
00:05:24,575 --> 00:05:25,742
Why do you have his jump drive?

111
00:05:25,743 --> 00:05:27,411
- I needed it.
- For what?

112
00:05:31,874 --> 00:05:34,167
See, I think you needed it
to make a copy of the drive you got

113
00:05:34,168 --> 00:05:36,837
from Anna Merrick
before she killed herself on the train.

114
00:05:38,047 --> 00:05:40,465
Where is that thumb drive?

115
00:05:40,466 --> 00:05:42,175
I have no idea what you're talking about.

116
00:05:42,176 --> 00:05:44,635
You're the only one
that came into contact with her,

117
00:05:44,636 --> 00:05:46,638
and the drive was not on her person.

118
00:05:47,806 --> 00:05:49,057
Do you think we're stupid?

119
00:05:49,058 --> 00:05:50,142
Yes.

120
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:55,022
Who was the woman in the park?

121
00:05:56,106 --> 00:05:58,901
You know, the one that you let
open the drive and look at the contents?

122
00:06:01,653 --> 00:06:02,988
Where is she?

123
00:06:03,697 --> 00:06:05,406
Let me guess.

124
00:06:05,407 --> 00:06:07,408
You spent most of your resources on me
'cause you thought

125
00:06:07,409 --> 00:06:09,368
I'd be the problem and she'd be easy.

126
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:12,830
Then, after I was drugged,
you went back for her but she was gone.

127
00:06:12,831 --> 00:06:14,958
Gave one of your junior officers the slip.

128
00:06:16,126 --> 00:06:18,252
You the one that was supposed
to be looking after her, Blynken?

129
00:06:18,253 --> 00:06:20,171
You look like the kind of jackass
who would get caught

130
00:06:20,172 --> 00:06:22,465
with his pants down and thumb up his ass.

131
00:06:22,466 --> 00:06:23,925
How about I put my foot up your ass?

132
00:06:23,926 --> 00:06:25,718
Try it.

133
00:06:25,719 --> 00:06:27,221
Not now.

134
00:06:28,305 --> 00:06:30,181
Okay, we get it.

135
00:06:30,182 --> 00:06:32,016
You're a tough guy.

136
00:06:32,017 --> 00:06:33,684
We read your jacket.

137
00:06:33,685 --> 00:06:35,186
[pulsing music playing]

138
00:06:35,187 --> 00:06:36,771
But what about your friends out there?

139
00:06:36,772 --> 00:06:38,356
They're not my friends.

140
00:06:38,357 --> 00:06:39,857
I just met 'em today.

141
00:06:39,858 --> 00:06:42,110
You and Officer Merrick
were running around with the drive

142
00:06:42,111 --> 00:06:45,404
and we saw you conversing with
Detective Green before we detained you.

143
00:06:45,405 --> 00:06:48,366
Now, we can only assume

144
00:06:48,367 --> 00:06:50,576
that they are coconspirators.

145
00:06:50,577 --> 00:06:52,495
We wanted to talk to you first
because we thought

146
00:06:52,496 --> 00:06:54,539
you might want to play ball
and spare them some pain,

147
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:56,708
but apparently you don't give a shit
what happens to them.

148
00:07:02,673 --> 00:07:04,799
No one knows the three of you are here.

149
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:07,260
We are treating you
like enemy combatants on U.S. soil.

150
00:07:07,261 --> 00:07:09,012
We can do whatever we want.

151
00:07:10,389 --> 00:07:12,306
Now, you...

152
00:07:12,307 --> 00:07:13,809
might be able to take it.

153
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:16,812
For a while.

154
00:07:18,522 --> 00:07:20,607
But how do you think they'll hold up?

155
00:07:25,779 --> 00:07:27,446
Get him out of here.
Bring me the woman.

156
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:28,949
Okay.

157
00:07:30,325 --> 00:07:32,201
Okay what?

158
00:07:32,202 --> 00:07:33,704
I'll answer your questions.

159
00:07:38,167 --> 00:07:39,668
That's better.

160
00:07:41,503 --> 00:07:43,463
So, why don't we try this again.

161
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:47,551
Where is the drive that Anna Merrick
gave to you on the train?

162
00:07:49,344 --> 00:07:50,637
[grunting]

163
00:08:22,628 --> 00:08:24,129
Told you.

164
00:08:37,226 --> 00:08:38,810
[intriguing music playing]

165
00:08:43,398 --> 00:08:46,817
It sounded like an all-out brawl
in there but now it's silent.

166
00:08:46,818 --> 00:08:48,445
Shit.

167
00:08:51,365 --> 00:08:53,075
[CIA officer] <i>Hello? Hello?</i>

168
00:08:56,119 --> 00:08:58,537
[Jacob] Holy shit.

169
00:08:58,538 --> 00:09:00,790
We thought they were kicking your ass.

170
00:09:00,791 --> 00:09:02,668
[Tamara] Where you going?

171
00:09:04,378 --> 00:09:05,879
Did he just leave us?

172
00:09:09,758 --> 00:09:11,260
[car alarm chirps]

173
00:09:22,729 --> 00:09:24,856
[phone ringing]

174
00:09:32,322 --> 00:09:34,156
- Hold that.
- All right.

175
00:09:34,157 --> 00:09:35,908
Phone means what I think it means?

176
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:37,411
Company'll be here soon.

177
00:09:39,121 --> 00:09:40,622
[phone stops ringing]

178
00:09:41,832 --> 00:09:43,332
Maybe it's just a wrong number.

179
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:45,043
[cell phones ringing]

180
00:09:46,295 --> 00:09:48,170
They're calling cell phones now.
More than one.

181
00:09:48,171 --> 00:09:49,588
Means more than one guy's coming.

182
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:52,383
- You get their guns?
- There were none. Must be locked up.

183
00:09:52,384 --> 00:09:54,302
They didn't think they needed
'em with you in cuffs.

184
00:09:54,303 --> 00:09:55,429
They were wrong.

185
00:09:56,555 --> 00:09:58,390
Okay. Try that.

186
00:10:03,186 --> 00:10:04,729
Your wallets are on the table
in the other room.

187
00:10:04,730 --> 00:10:06,314
[Tamara] Got it.

188
00:10:06,315 --> 00:10:07,691
[phones continue ringing]

189
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:13,447
Jesus.

190
00:10:25,167 --> 00:10:26,751
[grunts]

191
00:10:26,752 --> 00:10:28,295
They'll leave a message.

192
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:31,964
- [grunting]
- We're running out of time!

193
00:10:31,965 --> 00:10:33,674
Just a little more.

194
00:10:33,675 --> 00:10:35,177
You're gonna have to squeeze through.

195
00:10:37,554 --> 00:10:39,765
[grunts] I-I think I'm stuck.

196
00:10:46,897 --> 00:10:48,398
[Reacher] Go. Back down, back down.

197
00:10:57,824 --> 00:10:59,326
Close the door.

198
00:11:02,245 --> 00:11:03,622
Go, go, go!

199
00:11:05,832 --> 00:11:07,292
[grunts]

200
00:11:19,221 --> 00:11:20,514
[wheels screeching in distance]

201
00:11:24,434 --> 00:11:25,768
There's more of 'em?

202
00:11:25,769 --> 00:11:27,521
To the alley.

203
00:11:45,956 --> 00:11:47,249
Get in!

204
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:51,252
{\an8}I'm not CIA! My van has cats on it!

205
00:11:51,253 --> 00:11:52,421
[gunshots]

206
00:11:54,047 --> 00:11:55,215
Go!

207
00:11:59,594 --> 00:12:01,178
Who are you?

208
00:12:01,179 --> 00:12:03,806
Russell Plum. Freelance journalist.

209
00:12:03,807 --> 00:12:05,141
- [Jacob] Hey, look out!
- [van honks]

210
00:12:05,142 --> 00:12:06,475
[Russell] Oh, shit!

211
00:12:06,476 --> 00:12:08,185
[cars honking]

212
00:12:08,186 --> 00:12:11,105
I saw 'em bring you in on a gurney
yesterday, and you two

213
00:12:11,106 --> 00:12:13,399
were carried in a few hours later.
I've been watching that building

214
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:14,817
- for weeks.
- Why?

215
00:12:14,818 --> 00:12:17,403
Figured it was a CIA black site,
and I was right.

216
00:12:17,404 --> 00:12:19,071
Saw you trying to escape, I came to help.

217
00:12:19,072 --> 00:12:20,573
What the hell for?

218
00:12:20,574 --> 00:12:23,492
For my story. We are gonna blow the lid
off what's going on in there.

219
00:12:23,493 --> 00:12:24,995
What's going on in there?

220
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:28,372
- Answer the man.
- Me? I don't know.

221
00:12:28,373 --> 00:12:30,332
[Tamara] Well, what the fuck was your
sister involved in that I got snatched

222
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:32,751
- by the goddamn CIA?
- I have no idea.

223
00:12:32,752 --> 00:12:35,421
Anna worked for the Pentagon,
so whatever's on the jump drives

224
00:12:35,422 --> 00:12:37,381
they're looking for
has to be military related.

225
00:12:37,382 --> 00:12:38,883
We need to know for sure.

226
00:12:38,884 --> 00:12:40,050
How are we gonna find out?

227
00:12:40,051 --> 00:12:43,429
I have someone who can help.
Just got to get down to DC.

228
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:47,266
Down to D.C.?
Look out your window, man.

229
00:12:47,267 --> 00:12:48,852
We are in D.C.

230
00:12:49,853 --> 00:12:51,437
[uneasy music playing]

231
00:12:51,438 --> 00:12:53,398
What is going on?

232
00:13:01,656 --> 00:13:03,158
[tires screeching]

233
00:13:19,132 --> 00:13:22,301
I'm investigating
the world's most secretive agency.

234
00:13:22,302 --> 00:13:23,803
I use precaution.

235
00:13:31,478 --> 00:13:33,146
- [keys jingling]
- [lock clicks]

236
00:13:44,991 --> 00:13:46,701
Pen is mightier than the sword.

237
00:13:47,911 --> 00:13:49,453
Depends on who's wielding the sword.

238
00:13:49,454 --> 00:13:51,956
[Russell] All I need is a pen. You'll see.

239
00:13:51,957 --> 00:13:53,832
- [Tamara] What is all this?
- [Russell] My research.

240
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:55,460
Been investigating the CIA for years.

241
00:13:56,336 --> 00:13:58,003
- Because?
- Because they're involved

242
00:13:58,004 --> 00:14:00,464
in all kinds of shady shit that
the public needs to know about.

243
00:14:00,465 --> 00:14:03,342
They trained Manson, covered up Kennedy,

244
00:14:03,343 --> 00:14:05,344
got me fired from <i>The Washington Post.</i>

245
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:07,054
Now I just have to prove all of it.

246
00:14:07,055 --> 00:14:08,222
You wrote for the <i>Post?</i>

247
00:14:08,223 --> 00:14:11,308
<i>Post.</i> Then the <i>Examiner.</i>
Then the <i>Washington City Paper.</i>

248
00:14:11,309 --> 00:14:13,269
Then a few free periodicals.

249
00:14:13,270 --> 00:14:14,645
None of 'em wanted the truth.

250
00:14:14,646 --> 00:14:17,147
They're all beholden to their
corporate and political overlords.

251
00:14:17,148 --> 00:14:20,109
Now I'm strictly Internet-based.

252
00:14:20,110 --> 00:14:23,112
I give it directly to the people.

253
00:14:23,113 --> 00:14:24,614
No filters.

254
00:14:26,616 --> 00:14:28,158
[Jacob] Holy shit.

255
00:14:28,159 --> 00:14:31,036
Hey, we're across the street
from the CIA building.

256
00:14:31,037 --> 00:14:33,706
Stay away from the windows.

257
00:14:33,707 --> 00:14:34,873
Are we safe here?

258
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:36,875
Probably.

259
00:14:36,876 --> 00:14:38,544
They know we got away in a vehicle.

260
00:14:38,545 --> 00:14:40,588
It's unlikely they'd look for us
on their own block.

261
00:14:40,589 --> 00:14:42,715
Yeah, I circled around the back
and came in through the rear entrance.

262
00:14:42,716 --> 00:14:45,343
Nobody knows we're here.
Hey, you want to watch 'em?

263
00:14:46,344 --> 00:14:48,887
I hid cameras all over the roof.

264
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:50,599
Check this out.

265
00:14:52,559 --> 00:14:53,935
That's you.

266
00:14:54,686 --> 00:14:57,605
Most people who work for the CIA
don't know where the black sites are.

267
00:14:57,606 --> 00:14:58,731
How do you know?

268
00:14:58,732 --> 00:15:01,442
Well, I traced payments
for construction work

269
00:15:01,443 --> 00:15:03,694
done on one of the exposed
overseas black sites

270
00:15:03,695 --> 00:15:05,321
through a maze of shell companies.

271
00:15:05,322 --> 00:15:08,032
Now, one of those shells

272
00:15:08,033 --> 00:15:10,618
was connected to an LLC
that has no visible income

273
00:15:10,619 --> 00:15:12,745
but somehow was able to purchase
that building across the street.

274
00:15:12,746 --> 00:15:15,080
- So...
- [tapping monitor]

275
00:15:15,081 --> 00:15:16,915
I looked at a map...

276
00:15:16,916 --> 00:15:18,459
and check this out.

277
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:21,837
It's over one of the old steam tunnels
that runs under Embassy Row.

278
00:15:21,838 --> 00:15:25,132
There has to be an illegal
CIA spy op, right?

279
00:15:25,133 --> 00:15:28,677
So, got a sweet off-the-books deal
for this loft

280
00:15:28,678 --> 00:15:30,846
because the building is...

281
00:15:30,847 --> 00:15:32,598
well, it's technically condemned.

282
00:15:32,599 --> 00:15:35,017
Landlord's fighting it in court
but he's desperate for cash flow.

283
00:15:35,018 --> 00:15:36,477
Set up shop and I started watching.

284
00:15:36,478 --> 00:15:38,604
And then I see 'em

285
00:15:38,605 --> 00:15:41,523
bringing in steel plating
and welding equipment.

286
00:15:41,524 --> 00:15:44,735
I assume it was for cages.

287
00:15:44,736 --> 00:15:46,904
Right? Did they lock you guys in cages?

288
00:15:46,905 --> 00:15:49,365
Yeah. For a while.

289
00:15:49,366 --> 00:15:50,908
I knew it.

290
00:15:50,909 --> 00:15:53,118
I'm gonna blow the lid off this thing.

291
00:15:53,119 --> 00:15:54,912
I'm gonna win my Pulitzer.

292
00:15:54,913 --> 00:15:57,164
I'm gonna need your testimony.

293
00:15:57,165 --> 00:15:58,415
No.

294
00:15:58,416 --> 00:16:01,460
But... I rescued you.

295
00:16:01,461 --> 00:16:03,754
You need to forget you ever met us.

296
00:16:03,755 --> 00:16:05,924
You've stumbled into something
way bigger than you can handle.

297
00:16:07,467 --> 00:16:08,842
- My story i--
- [Tamara] People already

298
00:16:08,843 --> 00:16:10,845
died over this, Russell.
You don't want to be next.

299
00:16:12,430 --> 00:16:14,224
Okay. What do we do now?

300
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:16,517
We?

301
00:16:16,518 --> 00:16:19,061
I thought you were just gonna ride it out
till you get your pension.

302
00:16:19,062 --> 00:16:22,314
I was drugged and taken
150 miles from my home.

303
00:16:22,315 --> 00:16:23,691
I'm in this shit now.

304
00:16:23,692 --> 00:16:26,360
Public transportation's risky
with the CIA looking for us.

305
00:16:26,361 --> 00:16:28,779
My sister was on the train in Philly.

306
00:16:28,780 --> 00:16:30,614
So her car's still
got to be in her garage.

307
00:16:30,615 --> 00:16:31,865
She lived near here.

308
00:16:31,866 --> 00:16:33,992
They've probably
ransacked the place already.

309
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:36,662
Odds are it's safe to go.
Keep your heads on a swivel.

310
00:16:36,663 --> 00:16:37,746
[Tamara] What are you gonna do?

311
00:16:37,747 --> 00:16:38,997
Go look for John Sampson.

312
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:41,959
The congressman? What the hell
does he have to do with this?

313
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,460
That's what I'm gonna find out.

314
00:16:43,461 --> 00:16:44,837
- These burners?
- [Russell] Yeah.

315
00:16:44,838 --> 00:16:46,089
Help yourself.

316
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:48,716
I've already memorized your numbers.

317
00:16:48,717 --> 00:16:50,175
I'll text you mine.

318
00:16:50,176 --> 00:16:51,218
Call me after you get the car.

319
00:16:51,219 --> 00:16:52,470
What do you want me to do?

320
00:16:55,724 --> 00:16:57,600
Start looking for a new place to live.

321
00:17:00,478 --> 00:17:01,980
Man.

322
00:17:03,481 --> 00:17:05,483
[foreboding music playing]

323
00:17:20,582 --> 00:17:23,418
- [metal detector warbling]
[guard] Step forward.

324
00:17:42,854 --> 00:17:44,563
Is Representative Sampson in today?

325
00:17:44,564 --> 00:17:46,190
Yes, he is. And you are?

326
00:17:46,191 --> 00:17:47,733
A constituent.

327
00:17:47,734 --> 00:17:50,402
I'm sorry, sir. His schedule is full.

328
00:17:50,403 --> 00:17:52,029
May I take your name?

329
00:17:52,030 --> 00:17:53,655
How about I just write him a note?

330
00:17:53,656 --> 00:17:55,158
Of course.

331
00:18:09,923 --> 00:18:12,383
Tell him I'll be at the food trucks
by the National Mall.

332
00:18:39,327 --> 00:18:41,037
[Tamara] Someone was
looking for the drive.

333
00:18:49,254 --> 00:18:51,089
Your nephew?

334
00:18:54,050 --> 00:18:56,093
Yeah, wish he'd call me back.

335
00:18:56,094 --> 00:18:57,595
Starting to worry.

336
00:19:00,098 --> 00:19:02,641
You know college kids.

337
00:19:02,642 --> 00:19:05,144
I'd go days before calling my mom back.

338
00:19:10,483 --> 00:19:12,569
There's the garage. I'll get the keys.

339
00:19:21,077 --> 00:19:22,661
Hey, they're not here.

340
00:19:22,662 --> 00:19:23,912
[door opens]

341
00:19:23,913 --> 00:19:25,415
Forget the keys.

342
00:19:27,625 --> 00:19:28,834
Where's the car?

343
00:19:28,835 --> 00:19:30,419
I don't know.

344
00:19:30,420 --> 00:19:32,422
[door closes]

345
00:19:33,715 --> 00:19:37,134
Anna's Pentagon employee badge is here.

346
00:19:37,135 --> 00:19:40,178
Under some mail. Old mail.

347
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:42,056
Like she hasn't used it in a few weeks.

348
00:19:43,141 --> 00:19:45,267
Your sister must have left in a hurry.

349
00:19:45,268 --> 00:19:46,644
Didn't even finish her meal.

350
00:19:50,481 --> 00:19:52,983
Fuck.

351
00:19:52,984 --> 00:19:54,360
Still warm.

352
00:19:58,072 --> 00:20:00,074
[grunting]

353
00:20:25,099 --> 00:20:26,100
[shouts]

354
00:20:27,435 --> 00:20:28,728
[groans]

355
00:20:31,272 --> 00:20:32,439
Thank you.

356
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:34,108
Just returning the favor.

357
00:20:53,086 --> 00:20:56,088
Major Reacher. Don't get up.

358
00:20:56,089 --> 00:20:58,715
I'm Elspeth Sampson,
the congressman's wife.

359
00:20:58,716 --> 00:21:01,051
This is our head of security, Springfield.

360
00:21:01,052 --> 00:21:03,303
Smart move,
leaving your full name and rank

361
00:21:03,304 --> 00:21:05,722
so we could look you up,
know who we're dealing with.

362
00:21:05,723 --> 00:21:07,266
Otherwise we might not have come.

363
00:21:08,518 --> 00:21:10,435
[Elspeth] You said you were
one of John's constituents,

364
00:21:10,436 --> 00:21:12,521
but records don't show
a North Carolina address.

365
00:21:12,522 --> 00:21:14,064
Or any address.

366
00:21:14,065 --> 00:21:16,984
Don't have one. I served
in North Carolina three times, though,

367
00:21:16,985 --> 00:21:18,403
so I figured that was close enough.

368
00:21:19,487 --> 00:21:21,530
I see.

369
00:21:21,531 --> 00:21:23,240
And why did you choose to meet here?

370
00:21:23,241 --> 00:21:24,992
Hadn't eaten since yesterday.

371
00:21:24,993 --> 00:21:26,076
Why not?

372
00:21:26,077 --> 00:21:28,538
'Cause I was drugged
and abducted by the CIA.

373
00:21:29,998 --> 00:21:31,499
Then you should finish your meal.

374
00:21:37,422 --> 00:21:40,424
Most scandals involve something
the wife doesn't know about.

375
00:21:40,425 --> 00:21:42,009
Sending you was a statement.

376
00:21:42,010 --> 00:21:44,553
John didn't send me.

377
00:21:44,554 --> 00:21:46,972
I wanted to see for myself
if you were worth his time

378
00:21:46,973 --> 00:21:49,516
or if this is just
some pathetic attempt at blackmail.

379
00:21:49,517 --> 00:21:52,811
I don't want anything
from your husband except the truth.

380
00:21:52,812 --> 00:21:55,605
A Pentagon clerk killed herself
in front of me, night before last.

381
00:21:55,606 --> 00:21:58,317
With John's name on her lips?

382
00:21:59,402 --> 00:22:01,571
- Basically.
- "Basically" doesn't cut it.

383
00:22:02,739 --> 00:22:05,115
Why do you think my husband
has anything to do with this?

384
00:22:05,116 --> 00:22:07,034
With respect, my questions concern matters

385
00:22:07,035 --> 00:22:08,702
your husband probably
wouldn't share with you,

386
00:22:08,703 --> 00:22:10,704
so even if I asked,
it's unlikely you'd know the answer.

387
00:22:10,705 --> 00:22:12,290
John and I have no secrets.

388
00:22:13,374 --> 00:22:14,751
Maybe.

389
00:22:21,090 --> 00:22:24,217
Hotel, few blocks from here.

390
00:22:24,218 --> 00:22:26,053
Congressman's speaking
at a dinner there tonight.

391
00:22:26,054 --> 00:22:27,554
He's in his suite now, preparing.

392
00:22:27,555 --> 00:22:29,890
He'll be expecting you.

393
00:22:29,891 --> 00:22:32,602
You get five minutes of his time,
not one second more.

394
00:22:37,398 --> 00:22:38,900
Can you give me a ride?

395
00:22:40,401 --> 00:22:41,985
I could.

396
00:22:41,986 --> 00:22:43,987
[vehicle doors close]

397
00:22:43,988 --> 00:22:45,490
[engine starts]

398
00:22:46,908 --> 00:22:48,910
[vehicle departs]

399
00:22:50,286 --> 00:22:52,829
[grunts]

400
00:22:52,830 --> 00:22:54,582
Yeah, that should hold him.

401
00:22:55,875 --> 00:22:58,543
I'll hold on to his Glock.

402
00:22:58,544 --> 00:23:00,045
You could use a weapon.

403
00:23:00,046 --> 00:23:02,006
Your sister keep any guns in the house?

404
00:23:04,425 --> 00:23:06,302
There's... the one.

405
00:23:07,929 --> 00:23:09,846
But she...

406
00:23:09,847 --> 00:23:12,682
Right. Sorry.

407
00:23:12,683 --> 00:23:14,685
[phone rings]

408
00:23:16,104 --> 00:23:18,773
If that was the CIA,
they'd be calling this guy's cell.

409
00:23:21,651 --> 00:23:23,653
Answer it. Pretend you're Anna.

410
00:23:25,029 --> 00:23:26,531
[ringing continues]

411
00:23:32,578 --> 00:23:33,996
Hello.

412
00:23:35,832 --> 00:23:37,582
This is she.

413
00:23:37,583 --> 00:23:38,793
No, he isn't.

414
00:23:40,002 --> 00:23:42,672
I have no idea.
But if I hear from him, I'll tell him.

415
00:23:44,674 --> 00:23:47,592
I really have to go.
I'm in the middle of something.

416
00:23:47,593 --> 00:23:49,095
Thank you for calling.

417
00:23:53,558 --> 00:23:55,768
That was one of Ben's football coaches.

418
00:23:57,812 --> 00:23:59,188
He never showed for practice.

419
00:24:08,156 --> 00:24:10,158
- [indistinct chatter]
- [piano playing gently]

420
00:24:15,454 --> 00:24:17,456
[elevator bell dings]

421
00:24:27,133 --> 00:24:28,467
<i>[knocking]</i>

422
00:24:31,512 --> 00:24:32,721
Snap.

423
00:24:32,722 --> 00:24:34,807
Come in, Reacher. We need to talk.

424
00:24:36,225 --> 00:24:39,102
Crackle. Pop.

425
00:24:39,103 --> 00:24:40,687
[Snap] Have a seat.

426
00:24:40,688 --> 00:24:43,149
No, thanks. Where's Sampson?

427
00:24:44,525 --> 00:24:45,734
You're in big trouble.

428
00:24:45,735 --> 00:24:48,195
You told us Anna Merrick didn't
say anything to you on the subway

429
00:24:48,196 --> 00:24:49,738
- the other night.
- She didn't.

430
00:24:49,739 --> 00:24:52,991
Well, that's not what you wrote in the
note that you sent to the congressman.

431
00:24:52,992 --> 00:24:55,202
You lied to federal investigators.

432
00:24:55,203 --> 00:24:56,703
People go to prison for that.

433
00:24:56,704 --> 00:24:58,580
- Not me.
- [Snap] Why not?

434
00:24:58,581 --> 00:25:01,666
You didn't identify yourselves.
You could've been anybody.

435
00:25:01,667 --> 00:25:04,419
So, if we showed you some ID
you would have told us the truth?

436
00:25:04,420 --> 00:25:05,670
Sure.

437
00:25:05,671 --> 00:25:08,758
So... did she say John Sampson's name?

438
00:25:10,092 --> 00:25:11,092
No.

439
00:25:11,093 --> 00:25:12,802
Then where did you hear it?

440
00:25:12,803 --> 00:25:14,387
From the CIA.

441
00:25:14,388 --> 00:25:15,889
When did you talk to the CIA?

442
00:25:15,890 --> 00:25:17,141
When they kidnapped me.

443
00:25:21,479 --> 00:25:23,188
Why would the CIA kidnap you?

444
00:25:23,189 --> 00:25:24,689
They think I know something.

445
00:25:24,690 --> 00:25:25,774
Do you?

446
00:25:25,775 --> 00:25:27,651
I know they're running
an illegal black site

447
00:25:27,652 --> 00:25:29,945
out of an old building
on the corner of Hopkins and P.

448
00:25:29,946 --> 00:25:31,655
Go see for yourselves.

449
00:25:31,656 --> 00:25:35,158
The way I see it, the CIA
knows way more about this than I do.

450
00:25:35,159 --> 00:25:36,701
If you have questions, ask them.

451
00:25:36,702 --> 00:25:38,036
You want some advice?

452
00:25:38,037 --> 00:25:39,120
No.

453
00:25:39,121 --> 00:25:41,498
You were in the wrong place
at the wrong time

454
00:25:41,499 --> 00:25:42,958
and you saw the wrong thing.

455
00:25:42,959 --> 00:25:45,001
Something fucked-up
happened in front of you

456
00:25:45,002 --> 00:25:47,003
and, as a former investigator,
you want to look into it

457
00:25:47,004 --> 00:25:49,589
'cause your instincts
say that things don't smell right.

458
00:25:49,590 --> 00:25:53,635
But this is not a case you're gonna close.

459
00:25:53,636 --> 00:25:55,303
Walk away.

460
00:25:55,304 --> 00:25:57,847
'Cause if you keep sticking your nose
where it doesn't belong,

461
00:25:57,848 --> 00:25:59,516
you're gonna get it cut off.

462
00:25:59,517 --> 00:26:01,519
[tense music playing]

463
00:26:12,488 --> 00:26:14,239
- [Tamara] <i>Yeah.</i>
- Have any trouble?

464
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:16,491
Nothing we couldn't handle.
What about you?

465
00:26:16,492 --> 00:26:18,702
Same. Need you to pick me up.

466
00:26:18,703 --> 00:26:21,288
Can't. Anna's car isn't here.

467
00:26:21,289 --> 00:26:22,915
Had Docherty put out a BOLO.

468
00:26:24,041 --> 00:26:26,126
<i>Federal agents could have
taken the car to search it.</i>

469
00:26:26,127 --> 00:26:27,711
Maybe.

470
00:26:27,712 --> 00:26:29,045
<i>But they tossed the house.</i>

471
00:26:29,046 --> 00:26:30,714
<i>Probably could have searched
the car in the garage at the same time.</i>

472
00:26:30,715 --> 00:26:32,132
Maybe it was stolen.

473
00:26:32,133 --> 00:26:33,508
That'd be quite a coincidence.

474
00:26:33,509 --> 00:26:34,968
<i>Coincidences are rare.</i>

475
00:26:34,969 --> 00:26:38,638
So what we're left with
is Anna drove her car to Philly.

476
00:26:38,639 --> 00:26:40,640
Then, for some reason,

477
00:26:40,641 --> 00:26:43,018
got out and got on the subway.

478
00:26:43,019 --> 00:26:45,437
- Why would she do that?
<i>- No idea.</i>

479
00:26:45,438 --> 00:26:47,105
Anything else?

480
00:26:47,106 --> 00:26:49,065
Ben missed football practice.

481
00:26:49,066 --> 00:26:50,734
<i>He's on scholarship.</i>

482
00:26:50,735 --> 00:26:52,527
<i>Knows if he screws up, he'll lose it.</i>

483
00:26:52,528 --> 00:26:54,904
<i>I don't care what
that woman he met looks like,</i>

484
00:26:54,905 --> 00:26:58,033
<i>he's not risking his full ride
for any girl.</i>

485
00:26:58,034 --> 00:27:00,619
We've got to get back to Philly
and find him.

486
00:27:01,704 --> 00:27:03,038
Public transpo's out.

487
00:27:03,039 --> 00:27:04,247
<i>We need a car.</i>

488
00:27:04,248 --> 00:27:06,542
I know someone
who has a car we can borrow.

489
00:27:08,627 --> 00:27:09,627
You're back.

490
00:27:09,628 --> 00:27:10,879
Anybody see you come in?

491
00:27:10,880 --> 00:27:12,505
- I came in the back.
- Good.

492
00:27:12,506 --> 00:27:15,175
'Cause two guys in suits
driving a sedan with government plates

493
00:27:15,176 --> 00:27:16,843
just pulled into the black site.

494
00:27:16,844 --> 00:27:20,221
Wouldn't be CIA with those plates,
but I don't know.

495
00:27:20,222 --> 00:27:23,391
Could be FBI or NSA, but they like to use
generic state plates, not draw attention,

496
00:27:23,392 --> 00:27:26,519
so my guess is that they're DCSA,
maybe DCIS.

497
00:27:26,520 --> 00:27:29,147
Anyway, they kicked in the door,
they went inside.

498
00:27:29,148 --> 00:27:31,358
They're not gonna find anything,
because the CIA bugged out

499
00:27:31,359 --> 00:27:33,777
just before they got there.
There goes my story.

500
00:27:33,778 --> 00:27:35,820
Place is completely cleared out now.

501
00:27:35,821 --> 00:27:37,906
Wonder how they found out
about the black site.

502
00:27:37,907 --> 00:27:39,824
- I told 'em.
- Why would you do that?

503
00:27:39,825 --> 00:27:42,494
'Cause I want to give the CIA
something to worry about besides us.

504
00:27:42,495 --> 00:27:44,537
- Us?
- I need your help.

505
00:27:44,538 --> 00:27:46,289
I knew you'd come around.

506
00:27:46,290 --> 00:27:48,083
Okay, but before we go,
I need a new burner.

507
00:27:48,084 --> 00:27:50,794
For all I know, they grabbed the signal
off mine during my meeting with the feds.

508
00:27:50,795 --> 00:27:53,463
- Could be trying to track it right now.
- Let me just get my shit.

509
00:27:53,464 --> 00:27:56,174
And don't worry. I'm a valuable asset.
You'll see.

510
00:27:56,175 --> 00:27:57,801
I can dig up any information you need.

511
00:27:57,802 --> 00:28:00,011
You will not be sorry.

512
00:28:00,012 --> 00:28:02,555
I'm gonna need your full background
for my article.

513
00:28:02,556 --> 00:28:05,392
I mean, I can tell you're former military
by the way you carry yourself.

514
00:28:05,393 --> 00:28:07,685
And your pointed questions
and limited answers,

515
00:28:07,686 --> 00:28:11,523
well, makes me think
you're some kind of investigator.

516
